2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T14:17:43-07:00","id":594138,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to start the Descent vs Fallen argument again, but I do feel like Demon has been lacking SOMETHING for awhile now. Maybe its my love of LARPS or that I cut my teeth on Vampire for the WOD. For whatever reason, I like the political aspects of a WOD game most of all...and I don't feel Demon supports that gameplay style very well. That's one reason I made the Las Vegas setting (where the Unchained found a way to &quot;weaponize&quot; sin to drown out the will of the God-Machine in a &quot;signal to noise&quot; fashion- a single omniscient desire lost in the scream of a million petty human ones). I wanted to push the God-Machine a little out of the lime light and give the Demons a chance to make their own lives miserable. As such I welcome the Storyteller's Guide as long overdue resource for addressing my misgivings and helping me explore what the Demons might do if they aren't always looking over their shoulders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T08:49:18-07:00","id":594800,"title":"","content":"I always thought of the Qashmallim as being what the GM based his creations 