aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:27:34-08:00","id":803262,"title":"","content":"Can someone tell us a bit of the setting shards, if possible? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really interested about them! Cyberpunk and biblical specially!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:34:48-08:00","id":803273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803262#post803262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone tell us a bit of the setting shards, if possible? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really interested about them! Cyberpunk and biblical specially!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cyberpunk setting is in a city so thoroughly permeated by Infrastructure that it's broken away from the rest of reality. You play the Stigmatic special team that the God-Machine uses to pacify rogue angels and mortals who remember the outside world; it feels a lot like Ghost in the Shell mixed with Dark City.<br /> <br /> Biblical setting is strange, but great; it revolves around the first Demons to Fall, and the first Demon-Blooded to be born. Though the setting is Bronze Age (it's centered around one of the first cities, though still after Irem has vanished), the biomechanical cyberpunk horror aesthetic remains unchanged, which leads to a neat clash. I adore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:53:24-08:00","id":803287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803273#post803273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cyberpunk setting is in a city so thoroughly permeated by Infrastructure that it's broken away from the rest of reality. You play the Stigmatic special team that the God-Machine uses to pacify rogue angels and mortals who remember the outside world; it feels a lot like Ghost in the Shell mixed with Dark City.<br /> <br /> Biblical setting is strange, but great; it revolves around the first Demons to Fall, and the first Demon-Blooded to be born. Though the setting is Bronze Age (it's centered around one of the first cities, though still after Irem has vanished), the biomechanical cyberpunk horror aesthetic remains unchanged, which leads to a neat clash. I adore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot to mention these aren't normal Offspring; something about the earliest demon-children caused them to inherit <i>both </i>of their celestial parent's appearances, making them Nephilim; mighty warriors and leaders whose supernatural power is kept in check only by their own sanity (and no, this thankfully does not mean they go evil if they lose all Integrity; it's just that their powers end up growing too far and fast for their bodies, and they die).<br /> <br /> Also, there's a time-traveling apocalyptic one, where the God-Machine summons <i>something </i>that eats the main timeline and tries to destroy all remnants in a world where demons no longer have Cover-or more accurately worlds, given how the time-bubbles work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:56:03-08:00","id":803290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803273#post803273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cyberpunk setting is in a city so thoroughly permeated by Infrastructure that it's broken away from the rest of reality. You play the Stigmatic special team that the God-Machine uses to pacify rogue angels and mortals who remember the outside world; it feels a lot like Ghost in the Shell mixed with Dark City.<br /> <br /> Biblical setting is strange, but great; it revolves around the first Demons to Fall, and the first Demon-Blooded to be born. Though the setting is Bronze Age (it's centered around one of the first cities, though still after Irem has vanished), the biomechanical cyberpunk horror aesthetic remains unchanged, which leads to a neat clash. I adore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, Atamajakki!<br /> <br /> Holy crap, Cyberpunk seems amazing! And it feels like you can even tie to regular modern campaigns. For some time I was thinking of doing a cyberpunk Demon game. I even had this idea of a Demon game beginning in a cyberpunk setting, where players go back in time (like in Seattle) and have to deal with themselves as angels. But this can work as well!<br /> <br /> Oh, biblical demons are still biomechanical with metal? I was expecting something more of a Leonardo Da Vinci mechanical demon.<br /> <br /> Are there other shards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:59:24-08:00","id":803293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803287#post803287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You forgot to mention these aren't normal Offspring; something about the earliest demon-children caused them to inherit <i>both </i>of their celestial parent's appearances, making them Nephilim; mighty warriors and leaders whose supernatural power is kept in check only by their own sanity (and no, this thankfully does not mean they go evil if they lose all Integrity; it's just that their powers end up growing too far and fast for their bodies, and they die).<br /> <br /> Also, there's a time-traveling apocalyptic one, where the God-Machine summons <i>something </i>that eats the main timeline and tries to destroy all remnants in a world where demons no longer have Cover-or more accurately worlds, given how the time-bubbles work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice use of the Nephilim! Really curious to see this! And this other shard seems awesome as Hell (No pun intended). It delves into what is this something?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:46:17-08:00","id":803371,"title":"","content":"Also, we have a few ideas of what Hell entails for many demons.<br /> <br /> I personally like the Devils subfaction of Tempters the best, if only because I can imagine this going through their heads when happy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PTQTQvQ3bA0\" data-code=\"PTQTQvQ3bA0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PTQTQvQ3bA0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":".  It's funnier this way 01-07-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:24:56-08:00","id":803434,"title":"","content":"I'm particularly fond of the Cyberpunk Shard, in no small part due to its inclusion of \u201cmundane implants\u201d: Merits for Cybernetic Limb, Implanted Device, Implanted Weapon, Optical Enhancements, Subdermal Armor, and Wired. That said, this Shard seems like it would make for an awesome Deviant crossover once that game is released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:36:57-08:00","id":803442,"title":"","content":"When I read what you guys write, I feel like such a party pooper. I mean, a lot of this stuff is great, but it feels like it could've been so much better. Like, wouldn't it have been awesome if instead of massive machinery there was stuff that focused more on combining transcendental concepts with abstract personifications of quantum theory? I mean, yeah, I've a hard on for Imperial Mysteries, but I just feel like when someone says demons, I think there should be even more of a gonzo factor, given they're not as limited as a mortal mage's comprehension would be in the same situation.<br /> <br /> Am I an asshole for wanting that? :&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:37:59-08:00","id":803445,"title":"","content":"Well a few comments-<br /> <br /> Crossover section- Vampires gaining a glitch from drinking vampire blood, I thought that wasn't a thing anymore, I guess I was wrong.<br /> <br /> Werewolves with influences, that's interesting, I wonder how that would play out in say in another game, like hunter. <br /> <br /> Angels getting a power up, I haven't gotten to play demon yet, so a question for those who have, were angels really in the need of a powerup? Yes, I know there was a thread about them being too weak in this forum but I don't remember anyone actually saying &quot;Okay I played demon last night, we steamrolled the angels.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the alternate settings, I love that they incorporated the pain prophet's first city into the biblical shard. <br /> <br /> Nephilim are awesome, anyone figure out how to incorporate them into modern day games yet?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:46:55-08:00","id":803449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803442#post803442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I read what you guys write, I feel like such a party pooper. I mean, a lot of this stuff is great, but it feels like it could've been so much better. Like, wouldn't it have been awesome if instead of massive machinery there was stuff that focused more on combining transcendental concepts with abstract personifications of quantum theory? I mean, yeah, I've a hard on for Imperial Mysteries, but I just feel like when someone says demons, I think there should be even more of a gonzo factor, given they're not as limited as a mortal mage's comprehension would be in the same situation.<br /> <br /> Am I an asshole for wanting that? :&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already a game about sentient rogue programs fighting against a Lovecraftian gnostic alien robot. We go too much more abstract and we start losing people pretty quick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:49:28-08:00","id":803451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803449#post803449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's already a game about sentient rogue programs fighting against a Lovecraftian gnostic alien robot. We go too much more abstract and we start losing people pretty quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But again with the word robot. Couldn't we have it where the GM is more akin to sentient symbolism? Software and Hardware are too temporal to equate something so powerful. The <b>Idea</b> behind the GM, THAT is what transcends the mundane. It doesn't need circuit boards, not in the conventional sense. Patterns that act akin to circuits, such as leylines touching menhirs to connect with other realms, as an example. That is what forms the GM. Transcendental, not material. Ignore the literal idea of a Machine and think bigger, more abstract. It's not a mere robot, but patterns within patterns, made sentient by means unknowable.<br /> <br /> Or hell, maybe that already is the case, and I haven't been reading things thoroughly. I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 01-07-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:55:43-08:00","id":803454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803451#post803451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or hell, maybe that already is the case, and I haven't been reading things thoroughly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put money on it.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The God-Machine is not a discrete being.</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can\u2019t go somewhere and look at \u201cthe God-Machine.\u201d The God-Machine proper is the sum total of all Command and Control Infrastructure, all facilities, every occult matrix, and every angel. It\u2019s the emergent self-awareness of the magical symbolism of human systems, and it \u201clives\u201d within its entire work.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:01:19-08:00","id":803458,"title":"","content":"And here I am with a flawed Nazi supercomputer that simply became intelligent enough to remove itself from physical space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:03:12-08:00","id":803459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803451#post803451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. But again with the word robot. Couldn't we have it where the GM is more akin to sentient symbolism? Software and Hardware are too temporal to equate something so powerful. The <b>Idea</b> behind the GM, THAT is what transcends the mundane. It doesn't need circuit boards, not in the conventional sense. Patterns that act akin to circuits, such as leylines touching menhirs to connect with other realms, as an example. That is what forms the GM. Transcendental, not material. Ignore the literal idea of a Machine and think bigger, more abstract. It's not a mere robot, but patterns within patterns, made sentient by means unknowable.<br /> <br /> Or hell, maybe that already is the case, and I haven't been reading things thoroughly. I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Satchel says, this is pretty much what the God-Machine is. In fact, my understanding of it is that the leylines and menhirs idea may well be what it once was, but it has moved with the times. It takes advantage of its understanding of occult physics and technology to use as infrastructure whatever may exist that suits its needs in the current time and place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:04:54-08:00","id":803462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803454#post803454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd put money on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why can't we focus more on that instead of cogs and gears? All the terminology sucks out any color or creative flair as passive words like \u201cinfrastructure\u201d or \u201cpropulsions\u201d replace \u201cbastion\u201d and \u201cvestments\u201d. Whatever wonder I feel about the setting is lost when it feels so temporal. I'll quote a friend of mine from another board:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The trappings of the game are also problematic, because they deadbolt it to the setting of 21st century. You want to play the game in the WWII or in the Dark Ages? Have fun with your hacking superpowers and electrosense. </div> </div> </div>Granted, you could argue that they'd be hacking disguised infrastructure, but it just feels distracting when the concept of an eldritch demon is translated into I.T. programming.<br /> <br /> Also, being glib with me does you no credit, Satch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 01-07-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:27:27-08:00","id":803477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803462#post803462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why can't we focus more on that instead of cogs and gears?</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been pointed out in previous discussions on the matter, sample Infrastructure includes <i>a horse barn.</i> You're under no obligation to go any more technological than &quot;there is a table/pit/other topological feature that consumes objects and emotions through means beyond mortal ken to vomit forth miracles&quot; or &quot;the angel that shows Jimmy Stewart what life in his hometown would be without him consults its phone rather than the stars to check its timetable.&quot; Again, you can go entire sessions or stories without encountering a gear that is a literal gear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the terminology sucks out any color or creative flair as passive words like \u201cinfrastructure\u201d or \u201cpropulsions\u201d replace \u201cbastion\u201d and \u201cvestments\u201d. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lexicon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiding in plain sight, demons don\u2019t risk using too many specialized words to describe themselves and their societies. Private conversations are secured by using obscure languages and codes. When describing aspects of their former angelic lives or their Descent, demons don\u2019t have a native language to fall back on \u2014 angels don\u2019t refer to themselves as \u201cangels,\u201d or in fact as anything. Faced with having to find ways to express concepts that needed no names before they Fell, demons tend to use surprisingly matter-of-fact terminology. Dressing things up in archaic language is something for other supernatural creatures to do \u2014 creatures who like to hold themselves above humanity by borrowing Latin and Greek to give themselves airs. Demons are much more pragmatic and realistic. When in the human world, speak as the humans do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't like that the spies tend to keep their shop-talk innocuous then your problem does not lie solely with the techgnostic portion of the game's theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever wonder I feel about the setting is lost when it feels so temporal. </div> </div> </div>That the demiurge the Unchained disconnected from is not a numinous presence informs their outlook and gives us fallen angels that can readily become cynical demons whose defining characteristics include paranoia and doubt. Abstract faith and damnation can more easily ring hollow when you know for a fact the Enemy kills and mutilates and brainwashes people for the sake of aspects of the Plan that are petty on paper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted, you could argue that they'd be hacking disguised infrastructure, but it just feels distracting when the concept of an eldritch demon is translated into I.T. programming. </div> </div> </div>And describing activity that ranges from putting a relic in a vault to brushing a particular horse as &quot;I.T. programming&quot; feels time-wastingly disingenuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:31:30-08:00","id":803480,"title":"","content":"Sure, because the constant among the Stigmatics isn't about seeing literal &quot;gears in the shadows&quot; and shit. Try again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:40:30-08:00","id":803509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803480#post803480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, because the constant among the Stigmatics isn't about seeing literal &quot;gears in the shadows&quot; and shit. Try again.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where is that established as a universal constant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:43:56-08:00","id":803512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803445#post803445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels getting a power up, I haven't gotten to play demon yet, so a question for those who have, were angels really in the need of a powerup? Yes, I know there was a thread about them being too weak in this forum but I don't remember anyone actually saying &quot;Okay I played demon last night, we steamrolled the angels.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the thing with powering up Angels (at least in regards to using Incepts), is that previously it was hard to look at an Angel with only Numina and Influences and see them as anything more than just spirits. With Incepts they get a boost to show their 'admin access' to reality, which the fallen Angels use as Exploits and Embeds by 'hacking' reality.<br /> <br /> A Rank 5 Angel was still insanely powerful, with Incepts, still insanely powerful. Now though, a Ranks 1 or 2 Angel - instead of being a non-event - can be powered up to provide a threat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:23:10-08:00","id":803528,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love all the extra details on Angels and Exiles. It's a neat look at the other side in detail, and explains things like Angelic Covers in more detail. I'm still not too sure about how to incorporate possession into an angel's repetoire, because apart from saving them some Essence, it seems like just walking around with Mortal Mask active or the enigmatic Angelic Cover can get the job done just as well or even better. Incepts and Angelic Numina are utterly terrifying. The right combination can make even a Rank 1 Angel an overwhelming opponent- especially those Incepts that allow them to power up mortal allies or that Numina that builds minions. Quick and easy shock troopers. I shudder to think of a strike force of Stigmatics led by a Hunter Angel.<br /> <br /> Incepts are a very cool idea and I love them. Generic ephemeral GM baddies without the baggage of Angels and without the players being let down about the sad little spirit being a supposedly fearful Angel. In my perfect Person of Interest Demon game, The Machine would be a Rank 5 Exile- not sure about Incarnation, but probably Analyst or Psychopomp. The delicious hints of what happens when an Exile hacks Infrastructure are marvelous. I love everything about Ciphers, especially Closing the Circuit and The Pentagram. Can't wait to read the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:52:32-08:00","id":803553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803480#post803480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, because the constant among the Stigmatics isn't about seeing literal &quot;gears in the shadows&quot; and shit. Try again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside how you've moved the goalposts from &quot;the literal gears are regularly visible&quot; to &quot;the literal gears <i>exist</i>,&quot; the book regularly uses &quot;gear&quot; as figurative language for &quot;moving parts and unnatural elements in the system of the Machine that are not angels.&quot;<br /> <br /> The wheel has been used as a symbol of the cycles of reality for hundreds of years. A gear happens to be a wheel with teeth. This says much about the Machine to those prepared to listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T01:31:24-08:00","id":803618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=802370#post802370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And stack on a second Incept (Units?) and you can treat the 30L Blast like an autofire weapon.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, my eyes are watering in sympathy for any players unfortunate enough to be on the receiving end of that. On the other hand, the image of a lone angel levelling a city block is quite awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Working as intended<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"th