 meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T15:53:19-08:00","id":804076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804047#post804047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read the DSG's section of interlocks?</div> </div> </div> </div> no I totally ignored it that's why I commented about how much I like it. <br /> <br /> Sarcasm aside. My point is. I would have rather you know an example or 5 of merged exploits for an actual aspect of the game. <br /> But there's room for. Say. Crossover. Which is way more optional than the analysts ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T17:13:15-08:00","id":804126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804076#post804076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> no I totally ignored it that's why I commented about how much I like it. <br /> <br /> Sarcasm aside. My point is. I would have rather you know an example or 5 of merged exploits for an actual aspect of the game. <br /> But there's room for. Say. Crossover. Which is way more optional than the analysts ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the crossover section is one of the best parts. I get why you're sore, and feel for you, and I know we have different tastes, but that world building is awesome. How may people have analysts on the table? How often do they go loud? Now, how often are storytellers looking for plot hooks?<br /> <br /> Personally, I know I will get way more mileage out of crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T17:40:40-08:00","id":804145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804076#post804076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> no I totally ignored it that's why I commented about how much I like it.<br /> <br /> Sarcasm aside. My point is. I would have rather you know an example or 5 of merged exploits for an actual aspect of the game.<br /> But there's room for. Say. Crossover. Which is way more optional than the analysts ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of people like crossover material, I'm afraid. However, you want five examples of Interlock-style merged Exploits?<br /> <br /> Here you go. The power level is pretty crazy. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Absorption</b><br /> <br /> An Analyst can, with a touch, take away the supernatural abilities of others and use them herself.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Possession</i> and <i>Merge</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Presence + Occult + Primum \u2013 Defence + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Analyst instead loses access to all Exploits, including improvised ones, for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The power fails. The Analyst may try again, but each subsequent use suffers a -1 penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> For the duration of the scene, the demon may take a number of powers from the target equal to successes rolled \u2013 these vary by target but could include Embeds, Exploits, demonic form abilities, Numina, Supernatural Merits, vampiric Disciplines, etc. The target cannot use them while the Analyst can (substituting Aether for any costs in Willpower, Vitae, etc). This power cannot take away innate abilities, such an angels Incepts or Manifestations, or a vampire\u2019s ability to use Vitae to heal.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> In addition to the above, the target cannot use <i>any</i> supernatural abilities, including innate ones, for the rest of the scene. Ephemeral Beings are trapped in whatever state of Manifestation they are presently in.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Quantum Immortality</b><br /> <br /> </div> This power lets an Analyst temporally lock a person\u2019s body, protecting them from harm while allowing them freedom of action.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Stop</i> and <i>Frozen In Time</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Intelligence + Science + Primum (-Resolve)<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Analyst fails to create the quantum effect. Parts of the target\u2019s body are momentarily frozen in time while others are not, causing Aggravated damage equal to the Analyst\u2019 Primum.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The power fails. The Analyst may try again, but each subsequent use suffers a -1 penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> For a number of minutes equal to the demon\u2019s Primum, the target is immune to all harm (or any healing powers). Their body exists in an incredibly unstable quantum state, both frozen in time and active. They may take actions normally, though these actions cannot directly alter their body (shifting Covers or manifesting any demonic form abilities are therefore impossible).<br /> In addition, the target suffers from a glitch for the rest of the scene (even if they are not a demon).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The power lasts for an entire scene, though the Analyst can choose to end it prematurely.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Hellhole</b></div> <br /> In a horrific and tortuous show of power, an Analyst can force an enemy into a temporal pocket dimension\u2026 and set it alight.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Incendiary</i> and <i>Solitary Confinement</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Presence + Science + Primum \u2013 Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Analyst is instead pulled into her own trap, remaining caged and aflame for three turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The power fails. The Analyst may try again, but each subsequent use suffers a -1 penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The target disappears with a flash of light and strong smell of burning sulphur for a number of turns equal to successes rolled. The target is shunted into a pocket dimension filled with nothing but scorching flames. They take four lethal damage every turn. <br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Analyst may also send any individuals or objects in a four metre radius from the victim into the burning pocket dimension. Note they cannot pick and choose what is sent \u2013 it\u2019s all or nothing. <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Temporal Double</b></div> <br /> Analysts are well aware of splinter timelines. This power lets them use this knowledge to create a perfect double of a target by creating a splinter timeline.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Four Minutes Ago</i> and <i>Summon</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Intelligence + Streetwise + Primum<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Analyst fails to summon a temporal double, instead attracting the notice of the God-Machine and taking the Hunted Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The power fails. The Analyst may try again, but each subsequent use suffers a -1 penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Analyst can summon a double of a chosen target, which may include themselves, to aid them for a scene. This double is pulled from an alternate timeline. The double is identical in all respects (including equipment) and remains for four minutes, after which they (and all equipment) disappear. The target suffers a glitch for the rest of the scene, however, even if they are not a demon.<br /> <br /> If the double is killed, the original is not harmed, but watching yourself die automatically inflicts the Shaken Condition and is a Breaking Point for human characters.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The double may remain for the rest of the scene, though the Analyst can dismiss them at will.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Go-Go Gadget</b></div> <br /> All possible gadgets already exist <i>in potentia</i>. They simply require the right hardware and Aether to exist. When Going Loud, Analysts prefer to fast-forward to the completed product.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Deep Pockets</i> and <i>Living Installation</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>2 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Intelligence + Crafts + Primum<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Analyst accidentally produces a one-shot, designed by the Storyteller, that is not useful (and is likely directly harmful).<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The power fails. The Analyst may try again, but each subsequent use suffers a -1 penalty to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Analyst can pull a one-shot gadget (see <b>Flowers of Hell</b>) from their pocket (or similar container). The Gadget may contain any Embed or Exploit the demon presently possesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The gadget is not a one-shot.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T17:49:18-08:00","id":804151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804126#post804126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I think the crossover section is one of the best parts. I get why you're sore, and feel for you, and I know we have different tastes, but that world building is awesome. How may people have analysts on the table? How often do they go loud? Now, how often are storytellers looking for plot hooks?<br /> <br /> Personally, I know I will get way more mileage out of crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sore. I made a critique. I can't comment on the cross over or its contents. I didn't and won't read it. But I'm allowed to comment that despite really liking the book is have liked to see one addition . And im getting flak for having an opinion that isn't euphoric over all the contents. Maybe I thought. I dunno if there's a system there'd be an example of it being implanted like the rest of the book does a great job doing. And it's surprising that it's omitted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T18:04:41-08:00","id":804157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804151#post804151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sore. I made a critique. I can't comment on the cross over or its contents. I didn't and won't read it. But I'm allowed to comment that despite really liking the book is have liked to see one addition . And im getting flak for having an opinion that isn't euphoric over all the contents. Maybe I thought. I dunno if there's a system there'd be an example of it being implanted like the rest of the book does a great job doing. And it's surprising that it's omitted.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're absolutely allowed to critique. But if you haven't read it and refuse to do so, critiquing is not what you are doing. For my part, I'm not trying to give you flak, I'm just saying that many of us find the crossover section welcome an useful, and clearly OP knows that which is why they wrote it in. Take that as you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T19:25:36-08:00","id":804215,"title":"","content":"im not saying the crossover over content is bad. I won't speculate on that. My critique is that so much finite space is spared for another way to run the same supernatural creatures we've all seen and have access to. When a legitimate concept relative to standalone game is omitted. Out of an entire series of demon spanning books because I have them all in multiples. Is that I would have liked an example in the book so I can point a player to it instead of saying &quot; here read everything about interlocks that's been published to figure this out&quot;. <br /> It's fine for me. Because I've only story told demon. I've never played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T20:39:36-08:00","id":804239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=803773#post803773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike crossover. And was disappointed when so much of this book was dedicated to it. So I skipped all if it. That being said.<br /> <br /> This was the first book I've read mostly cover to cover. and my god it's beautiful. From cover, fiction, and new ideas. I'm certainly going to be eluding to the possibility of my players gaining the pentagram.<br /> Loving the angel power boost. In our last game my players pretty much curb stomped a hunter angel. There's so much of this book that's going to be used. It was well worth the like 18$ I spent.<br /> <br /> I really wished though it had included some examples of the analysts exploit ability. And a few more embeds/ exploits would have been nice.<br /> <br /> If anyone is on the fence about getting the guide. You're going to enjoy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that there's really that much dedicated to it. I mean, they touch on each gameline and its most important aspects in pretty short, minimalist bursts. The issue might be that even though they kept it brief, the CofD world has become expansive enough that even a brief crossover treatment is going to take up a few pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T23:23:58-08:00","id":804273,"title":"","content":"But these games already exist. Like they are right there with complete rules in legitimate books. Do you get my point? I didn't set out to buy an abridged copy of every cofd book I already own. The rules as written pretty much allow you to use one Dolan on another game. Without taking word count away from the themes of the game your interested to support the other products. <br /> When I buy a 12 pack of Coke. I literally want 12 cans of cola. Not 10 cans, 1 Sprite, 1 root beer. <br /> <br /> And In that moment when the decision is made to take focus off the core concepts of the game, it's own unique examples and content. For the sake of &quot; but these things exist to&quot; I won't have any part of it. I won't read or enjoy being told for the umpteenth time that it sucks to be an artificially created human and here's how to bring that in your game if you don't have the book. <br /> <br /> So my comment Says &quot; I don't like it's addition I didn't read the content. So I can't speculate. But here's everything else that is great and something id like to have seen&quot; bam. That's the extent of it. <br /> <br /> Instead of focusing on hey. this chick who hates PDFs and dislikes a fraction of it it's content. She still recommends that people get it. Luke now. Get it. The he book is wonderful for all of the content that I did read. <br /> <br /> You people couldn't care less about that. But I have to defend myself against an onslaught of replies from other fans and freelancers. Why do you think the genre is stagnant. Because to hell with people who don't fawn over every word written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T23:50:42-08:00","id":804282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804273#post804273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these games already exist. Like they are right there with complete rules in legitimate books. Do you get my point? I didn't set out to buy an abridged copy of every cofd book I already own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: Buying ten corebooks to run NPCs for a different game that alluded to most of these monsters in its corebook is a goddamn bananas expectation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You people couldn't care less about that. </div> </div> </div>Well yes, because you opened the post with a statement that you don't think a section that's been known about since the book's outline was shared on the company blog should exist and appear to have expected this to go unremarked upon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I have to defend myself against an onslaught of replies from other fans and freelancers. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the matter of overshare, no, you don't, and if you have no plans to change your mind it's actively detrimental to the thread and your personal experience to keep re-pinging the argument. Let it fade.<br /> <br /> <br /> Found the advice in Chapter 3 handy for sorting out a setting hack I've left to sit for a few months; ditto bits and pieces of the Shards.<br /> <br /> Somewhat confused about how gaining Essence through Parameters works, but I'm glad to see the concept slivers represent got some attention and it's interesting to see exile evolution added to the game's narrative toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T01:42:40-08:00","id":804294,"title":"","content":"I would also like to point out that the Crossover advice is mainly... crossover advice. Even if I have the Vampire Core that does not tell me, for instance, how Strix interact with Infrastructure. The Demon STG does. Neither the Demon nor Werewolf Core tell me what Demons usually think of Werewolf mythology. The Demon STG does. Furthermore, I get three interesting plot hooks for each supernatural type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:29:37-08:00","id":804472,"title":"","content":"So satchel what your saying I can have an opinion but keep it to myself because I shouldnt to be allowed to respond when I'm making a point? Classy. I didn't realize I had to be a good little girl here to. But I get boys. I'll leave you to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:34:05-08:00","id":804619,"title":"","content":"Welp, this thread got ugly fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:44:46-08:00","id":804629,"title":"","content":"What I don't get is how someone who dislikes PDFs doesn't see the advantage of not having to lug 10 large books around if you're running a crossover. <br /> <br /> Hardbacks are <i>heavy. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:58:03-08:00","id":804644,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's stop a second.<br /> <br /> I think we 'care' too much that Minty dislikes things.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, I disagree with her. More importantly, I think she presented her opinions in a wrong way-I think there's ways to say &quot;Because I dislike crossover, I skipped that section and wished it had been used for other things&quot; that doesn't come across so abrasively.* I admit to that.<br /> <br /> But you know, that happens when people keep needling her about stuff like this. I know I've contributed, again, I'll admit that! But we're pushing unnecessarily. We're turning the thread into a nest of thorns, and we don't need that. I also feel like we're ganging up on her, and that doesn't feel right to me.<br /> <br /> It's okay that she has these problems. It's okay that we disagree.<br /> <br /> It's not okay that we're getting....well, mean about it. So, you know.<br /> <br /> Let's stop. She's okay to not like things she comes across.<br /> <br /> *Presenting your opinions without being a dick is an important skill, regardless of who you are. How you say a thing is as important as what you say. Lesson all of us, myself included, could do with practicing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T13:12:21-08:00","id":804655,"title":"","content":"Agreed Sean. We have a difference of opinion on what the book should be and what's useful. Both sides have said their bit. There's zero reason to keep fighting about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T13:15:59-08:00","id":804657,"title":"","content":"Ack, Arc, Arc, call me Arc.<br /> <br /> Weird for forumites to use my name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:09:28-08:00","id":804733,"title":"","content":"This book is pretty neato.<br /> <br /> I'm about to read the cyberpunky setting and it has me wondering, do you think access to the city could be integrated into a conventional Demon game? One of my favorite things in the original demon books description of setting is that there's always an element of High Weirdness to a place which the God-Machine is tapping into. I wonder if access to Mechotropolis (is that what it's called?) could be linked to any particular setting on the planet.<br /> <br /> One thing that comes to mind is tying it to Seattle. I remember reading the idea in the Seattle setting book that the Time Splinters could be an occult matrix intended to grant access to a future timeline where the God-Machine's advanced cyborg servants could be sent back to kick Demons in the pants and stuff. That seems like one place one could use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:15:51-08:00","id":804739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804657#post804657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ack, Arc, Arc, call me Arc.<br /> <br /> Weird for forumites to use my name.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty pleased with the rest of the book. I like that Exiles are like free agents, they still have a directive, but they have ultimate latitude in fulfilling it. I'd been using the Exile Programs from the Matrix as a short hand up till now, but Exiled Angels are much more complex, and have many more storytelling potential. <br /> <br /> The Urban Legends are pretty nifty, and I like the world building that takes place there. Still have to make it through the shards though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:26:06-08:00","id":804748,"title":"","content":"Simulacra are terrifying. One of the things that occurred to me is that those Coffee Shop safehouse infrastructures throughout Seattle are probably staffed by Simulacra who might act as security when Demons want to get at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:45:08-08:00","id":804766,"title":"","content":"I had a thought, looking at the Shards. If Giants in the Earth actually happened, the GM probably has it stored away in the Apocalypse Vault as a dangerous time splinter. But then I got to thinking if it would really want to get rid of the investment that is The City. What if Mechopolis or whatever it's called isn't in the future, but running parallel to Earth? What if Mechopolis and The City are one and the same? I'm picturing it as basically the God-Machine's Heaven.<br /> <br /> Then I remembered the City Walker Merit in the GMC. What if this is a side effect of the Infrastructure keeping Mechopolis tucked away, or a means to allow Its Stigmatic paladins travel to and from The City? What if a Dramatic Failure doesn't send you to a nightmare realm, but to a heaven of steel and chrome?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T17:41:47-08:00","id":804849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804733#post804733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book is pretty neato.<br /> <br /> I'm about to read the cyberpunky setting and it has me wondering, do you think access to the city could be integrated into a conventional Demon game? One of my favorite things in the original demon books description of setting is that there's always an element of High Weirdness to a place which the God-Machine is tapping into. I wonder if access to Mechotropolis (is that what it's called?) could be linked to any particular setting on the planet.<br /> <br /> One thing that comes to mind is tying it to Seattle. I remember reading the idea in the Seattle setting book that the Time Splinters could be an occult matrix intended to grant access to a future timeline where the God-Machine's advanced cyborg servants could be sent back to kick Demons in the pants and stuff. That seems like one place one could use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a few approaches you could use - the shard approach is definitely a good one. You could also use the common videogame trope of the &quot;light world vs. dark world&quot; where the city exists as one of the &quot;true&quot; representations of the city and it represents the city you're in through the lens of complete GM control. It could essentially be the &quot;fallen world&quot; version of whatever place you're using with some quantum superposition weirdness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 01-09-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T17:50:14-08:00","id":804856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804849#post804849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a few approaches you could use - the shard approach is definitely a good one. You could also use the common videogame trope of the &quot;light world vs. dark world&quot; where the city exists as one of the &quot;true&quot; representations of the city and it represents the city you're in through the lens of complete GM control. It could essentially be the &quot;fallen world&quot; version of whatever place you're using with some quantum superposition weirdness.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever reason, the first thing that came to mind was changing what The Maw does in Fear Tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:21:44-08:00","id":804881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804657#post804657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ack, Arc, Arc, call me Arc.<br /> <br /> Weird for forumites to use my name.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a grown man now, son. Isn't this what you asked for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:30:20-08:00","id":804891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804657#post804657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ack, Arc, Arc, call me Arc.<br /> <br /> Weird for forumites to use my name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't include your name in the signature, is my advice. It avoids forum dissonance<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:34:24-08:00","id":804896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804881#post804881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a grown man now, son. Isn't this what you asked for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in that liminial space between being a child and being an adult.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, fuck, I'll probably always be in that twilight. Might even do some good with it. But that aside, as this subject goes, I've just barely started. I'm still only a step above glorified forumite.<br /> <br /> I dunno if I'll ever be comfortable with this particular group calling me by my real name, like my profession means something here. Maybe one day. But for now, I'm still mostly like y'all. Just, you know. A step or two higher up the ladder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804891#post804891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't include your name in the signature, is my advice. It avoids forum dissonance<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That might be wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-09-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T19:15:32-08:00","id":804923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All this speculation about Giants, Fear Tomorrow, and Seattle </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bd9BP2PkVMQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bd9BP2PkVMQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bd9BP2PkVMQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bd9BP2PkVMQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T19:19:25-08:00","id":804926,"title":"","content":"I think this fiction was absolutely amazing. I almost died when the intro fiction ended. When I realized each chapter fiction was gonna coninue off of it, I was excited. The story and characters (Mecha tree is tastin yer poopz!) Were really immersive. The two rank5+ cosmic angels were both ery cool on their own, but as a contrasted pair, was brilliant. It made me wish that the book addressed Archangels and Archdemons. I was really hoping for that in the Urban Legends. I'll admit, i didnt like the urban legends nearly as much as I thought i would, especially the Satan Signal :/ OTOH, I didnt think I'd love the angels/exiles/etc chapter nearly as much as I did. It really filled out angels to be more dimensional (even sympathetic). Echoes are seriously a creepy, delicious idea. And with the section on Hell and the existence of Lares, I have a way to pull off my demon-lord's Untouchable hellscape Nightclub that manages to avoid angels shutting it down. The crossover section was great (especially the little spoilers about Changeling, Geist, and Promethean 2e). I was glad to see so much addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:20:30-08:00","id":804960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804896#post804896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm in that liminial space between being a child and being an adult.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, fuck, I'll probably always be in that twilight. Might even do some good with it. But that aside, as this subject goes, I've just barely started. I'm still only a step above glorified forumite.<br /> <br /> I dunno if I'll ever be comfortable with this particular group calling me by my real name, like my profession means something here. Maybe one day. But for now, I'm still mostly like y'all. Just, you know. A step or two higher up the ladder.<br /> <br /> <br /> That might be wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's our secret, Art, nobody ever magically &quot;grows up&quot; everyone fakes it till they get experience that is unduly disregarded by the newer generations. Experience gathered with sweat and blood and tears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T23:30:11-08:00","id":805049,"title":"","content":"This really was an excellent book. I think Altered State was my favorite game hack/shard, but the sections on exiles, ciphers, and angels were also really great. <br /> The only thing that disappointed me was the Satan Signal, which I've been hyped about since Rose mentioned it way back on the Kickstarter. I was expecting something with more unsettling implications for the Unchained. Like I said, though - everything else was awesome. Loved the cosmic angels in the intro fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:43:40-08:00","id":805171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=804960#post804960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nobody ever magically &quot;grows up&quot; everyone fakes it till they get experience that is unduly disregarded by the newer generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>My whole life is flashing before my eyes now and it's not a good thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:26:07-08:00","id":805631,"title":"","content":"I agree on the Satan Signal. I truthfully wished that the weird bug-thing was one of the alternate versions, while the first alternate (about the Signal coming from the First fallen) couldve been the core version. I had been gleefully looking forward to it, but a demon-eating bug that causes falls? Granted, I was also hoping to see a legendary demon like Asmodeus, Belial, or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:25:06-08:00","id":805665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=805631#post805631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree on the Satan Signal. I truthfully wished that the weird bug-thing was one of the alternate versions, while the first alternate (about the Signal coming from the First fallen) couldve been the core version. I had been gleefully looking forward to it, but a demon-eating bug that causes falls? Granted, I was also hoping to see a legendary demon like Asmodeus, Belial, or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be frank: &quot;cryptids can develop functional invisibility to the God-Machine along with a power demons only know as an Exploit whose primary drawbacks are drawing the Machine's attention and not being sure where you'll come out&quot; is kind of of greater utility than &quot;what may be one of your character's long-term goals has already been accomplished by a stronger NPC when 'being subordinate to a stronger NPC' is essentially a universal background element for demons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:59:02-08:00","id":805687,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest; when I wrote the Satan Signal I initially did lean towards the first alternative, but I didn't want to canonise a Lucifer-analogue for <b>Demon: the Descent</b> because it felt a little too similar to Fallen (even though the concept of canon in CofD's toolkit world is a foggy one). I <i>love</i> the idea of a demon who ascended to become a ghost in the God-Machine, a virus within It that encourages angels to Fall, and if you do too you should use the hell out of it. It's also a really ambitious Hell that can fit, with some tweaks, all of the existing Agendas, if you fancy letting your PCs reach cosmic-tier.<br /> <br /> I also quite the idea that in a setting full of crazy conspiracies and mysteries the solution to one of the bigger, more intriguing ones is as mundane as a giant demon-eating monster (not that the Signaler is mundane) that'll probably just eat you if you ever discover the truth. I also love the hell out of cryptids - you're lucky cryptids aren't behind <i>every </i>urban legend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - and wanted to show just how powerful they can become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 01-10-2016, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:01:22-08:00","id":805828,"title":"","content":"Eremite and Satchel, those are very, very good points. I can definitely understand it better now--with limited wordcount, its more useful and spooky to have a demon eating cool cryptid, when something Luciferesque really should be more a rumor and as such only be covered briefly. I'd love to have heard a more detailed version of the ghost in the godmachine alternate. OTOH, I do like that cryptid as a whole. The way I'll probably run in is that demons think the satan signal is the first fallen, and he probably exists and does perpetuate the signal. But this Cryptid ALSO sends out a signal, and foolish, hopeful demons confused the two and call them both the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:19:07-08:00","id":805838,"title":"","content":"The Alternate Truth I'll probably end up using is the specialized Infrastructure for making demons fall according to the purposes of the God-Machine. I like that quite a bit better than a cryptid or a literal Lucifer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T01:04:59-08:00","id":805884,"title":"","content":"Actually, I feel rather silly for utterly fumbling the ball on this one. The Satan Signal I wanted IS in the book. I can basically take the alternative Satan Signal and graft it to the Cipher mechanics and fluff in chapter 1. I didnt get a tiny blurb on what I wanted for the Satan Signal, I got half a chapter on it.. Duh. Storyteller's guides, thats what they do. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T01:54:33-08:00","id":805905,"title":"","content":"Kind of embarrassed that it took me most of a week to make the obvious connection between the primary and secondary effects of the Delivery Incept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:25:48-08:00","id":805947,"title":"","content":"What do you mean? I gave one of my angels that incept strictly for the secondsry benefit. I mean, its a bit.. Beasty, sorta like their ability to break open doors and bless their kin.. is that it, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:28:59-08:00","id":805949,"title":"","content":"Damn it Onyx Path, your sorcerers have charmed the money out of my wallet again. I wasn't going to buy this book, since I don't have any plans to run Demon in the immediate future. As soon as I saw the announcement that it was released though I couldn't help myself, I bought and downloaded it straight away. I've only just had a quick scroll through but it looks great. Glad to see the section explaining Cyphers because to be perfectly honest I never understood that idea at all. The artwork and layout is beautiful. Just looking at this book gets me excited about Demon.<br /> <br /> ...maybe I can persuade one of my friends to run a game of Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:18:33-08:00","id":806148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=805947#post805947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? I gave one of my angels that incept strictly for the secondsry benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Delivery works to its fullest extent when used to summon/retrieve and enhance other ephemeral beings, which is an established course of action for the Machine to take.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are exiles still capable of using Incepts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:25:04-08:00","id":808328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=806148#post806148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are exiles still capable of using Incepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> Exiles haven't had their admin access revoked the way demons have, they're still ephemeral beings, they're still angels, they're just not getting command and communication from the G-m. They're basically Milton from Office Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:12:24-08:00","id":808547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=806148#post806148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are exiles still capable of using Incepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend the ST decides on a case-by-case basis. The level of Abandonment by the God-Machine varies - sometimes It cancels Incept privileges, sometimes it doesn't. There doesn't seem to be any discernible pattern to it. Wise demons are wary around Exiles; they can be dangerous foes, but also very useful allies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:33:18-08:00","id":808555,"title":"","content":"Can somebody give me examples of what Dynamic Covers do? Not quite sure how it works, especially given Force Relationship and...that one Embed that recontextualizes your cover in FoH exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:07:07-08:00","id":809131,"title":"","content":"Ok, am I the only one who is crazy enough ( with my friend who helps me ) who found latin in the book? I mean, does it have any meaning or not? It's the binary code near the text... or are we simply losing minds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:45:09-08:00","id":809166,"title":"","content":"The intro fiction to this book was amazing. For me it joins &quot;Some running night&quot; and &quot;Desert Dreaming Hunt&quot; as some of the CoD's best fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:37:25-08:00","id":809197,"title":"","content":"I bet Bunyip is happy to hear that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T00:31:43-08:00","id":810519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=808555#post808555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can somebody give me examples of what Dynamic Covers do? Not quite sure how it works, especially given Force Relationship and...that one Embed that recontextualizes your cover in FoH exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume you mean dynamic legend.<br /> <br /> You make a legend roll as normal, gaining access to things as normal, with two differences.<br /> <br /> 1) You can take a penalty to make the altered cover last a while<br /> <br /> 2) and you become a member of a &quot;tight knit community&quot;<br /> <br /> Essentially it's going undercover, &quot;Sure, I'm a mobster/vampire hunter/cultist of Great Old One/terrorist/whatever,&quot; and since it's a legend roll you can give yourself such things as allies, contacts, status ,or other stuff to fit the role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:35:20-08:00","id":810743,"title":"","content":"Dynamic Legend? Did I miss that somehow? I can't remember reading it in the STG","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:45:51-08:00","id":810750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=810743#post810743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynamic Legend? Did I miss that somehow? I can't remember reading it in the STG</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter Three, under the section on Insurgent games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:16:20-08:00","id":810862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=809166#post809166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The intro fiction to this book was amazing. For me it joins &quot;Some running night&quot; and &quot;Desert Dreaming Hunt&quot; as some of the CoD's best fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much. I am very pleased to hear that.<br /> <br /> In fact, thank you to everyone who has commented on the fiction. The fiction in these books is so rarely remarked upon, and the story is a bit out of left field, so I'm gratified to know so many people have taken the time to read it, and that they enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:57:13-08:00","id":812816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=808328#post808328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> Exiles haven't had their admin access revoked the way demons have, they're still ephemeral beings, they're still angels, they're just not getting command and communication from the G-m.<u><b> They're basically Milton from Office Space.</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just like to say really quick how much I like this comparison and how many weird looks I got after laughing at a Milton themed Exile in my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:14:43-08:00","id":812945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=810519#post810519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I presume you mean dynamic legend.<br /> <br /> You make a legend roll as normal, gaining access to things as normal, with two differences.<br /> <br /> 1) You can take a penalty to make the altered cover last a while<br /> <br /> 2) and you become a member of a &quot;tight knit community&quot;<br /> <br /> Essentially it's going undercover, &quot;Sure, I'm a mobster/vampire hunter/cultist of Great Old One/terrorist/whatever,&quot; and since it's a legend roll you can give yourself such things as allies, contacts, status ,or other stuff to fit the role.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how does it fit in when there are several Demon powers that do point 2? Is it just a matter that with the Dynamic Legend option, every demon has an option for it?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I might as well drop my questions about powers here.<br /> <br /> 1)Angelic Reflexes has no duration listed.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Roll Power + Finesse \u2013 Subterfuge to determine if the humans within the angel\u2019s range notice what the angel is seeking.&quot; - so can angels see through the eyes of every person affected by Translocation, or what? How do they get that information? Also, what exactly happens when someone uses Translocation and a Demon spoofs it? They register as human but still can't be moved (or seen through, as above)? How do angels register that one?<br /> <br /> 3)What's the essence cost for Incepts that have a primary ability without a listed cost, like Economy, Efficiency, Units, etc?<br /> <br /> 4)Is there a cap on how many essence you can spend for Scale's primary effect? Are you only limited to Numina when using it, or can you apply it to whatever dice pools and modifiers you wish?<br /> <br /> 5)I've been trying to be objective here while I'm asking questions, but I have to ask: you can seriously use Space to obviate someone's Defense? :/<br /> <br /> 6) How does Scale work with powers that do multiple things, like Angelic Reflexes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-20-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:42:06-08:00","id":812968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=812945#post812945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how does it fit in when there are several Demon powers that do point 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>aren't.</i> There are powers available that change <i>individual relationships</i>, but Force Relationship, Allies Into Gold, and Associate and Integrate all rely on changing the tenor of an existing connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:24:20-08:00","id":812993,"title":"","content":"I am up to the Tools of the Machine, and I am loving this thing. Enough to dress for the occasion.<br /> <br /> #madokaisachangelingdemoncrossover","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:28:56-08:00","id":812998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=812993#post812993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am up to the Tools of the Machine, and I am loving this thing. Enough to dress for the occasion.<br /> <br /> #madokaisachangelingdemoncrossover</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, it's a bit uncanny given my own recent change in wardrobe.<br /> <br /> How rad are those new angel bits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-20-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","