r":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:39:02-08:00","id":813045,"title":"","content":"One more quick question (at this rate I'm going to just create or resurrect a Demon &quot;Ask a simple question&quot; thread): Dynamic Legend says &quot;For every scene that the player wishes the altered Cover to remain in place \u2014 including the imitated Skills and Merits \u2014 subtract one die from the roll.&quot; - what roll is it referring to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:44:51-08:00","id":813048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=813045#post813045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more quick question (at this rate I'm going to just create or resurrect a Demon &quot;Ask a simple question&quot; thread): Dynamic Legend says &quot;For every scene that the player wishes the altered Cover to remain in place \u2014 including the imitated Skills and Merits \u2014 subtract one die from the roll.&quot; - what roll is it referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cover roll that you use to get stuff from Legend. The scene count is what prompts the &quot;snap back&quot; resolution of Undercover Identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:48:19-08:00","id":813052,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, Incepts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: No, actually, fuck that, oh my god, the <i>genres</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-20-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T19:04:29-08:00","id":813093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=813052#post813052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god, Incepts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: No, actually, fuck that, oh my god, the <i>genres</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That section was amazing from the very first draft. For me, one of the most awesome parts of freelancing is seeing people turn in stuff that is completely different from anything you would have ever considered but is actually even more amazing than what you expected to see. This was one of those for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:52:32-08:00","id":813150,"title":"","content":"I think the chapter &quot;Children of a Killer God&quot; made something click for me, and I have really started to see Angels and Exiles in the proper theological frame of mind. I'm not sure if it's the Incepts, the unique Numina, or something about the detail that was put into describing each Incarnation, but I stopped seeing them as processes and tools and started seeing them more as avatars or aspects of the Machine. An individual Angel could be seen as an avatar of the Infrastructure, and thus every aspect of the God-Machine is an Angel. It gave me a new frame of reference to think of how it treats Angels. <br /> <br /> How much effort do you put into an idea, or a routine, that works as expected? Do you really think of situational personas as different people? What would you do to rein in a thought that has careened off the tracks? How hard would you work to stamp out rogue aspects of your personality? I looked at the Machine, and I saw the Unchained writ large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-20-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T21:11:34-08:00","id":813157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=813150#post813150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the chapter &quot;Children of a Killer God&quot; made something click for me, and I have really started to see Angels and Exiles in the proper theological frame of mind. I'm not sure if it's the Incepts, the unique Numina, or something about the detail that was put into describing each Incarnation, but I stopped seeing them as processes and tools and started seeing them more as avatars or aspects of the Machine. An individual Angel could be seen as an avatar of the Infrastructure, and thus every aspect of the God-Machine is an Angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, between Mage 2e's <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9aFFCMGp1clN5YWc/view\" target=\"_blank\">Obrimos writeup spoiler</a> (&quot;To them, 'angels' are the names of natural laws&quot;) and <a href=\"http://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/116312026995/an-angel-is-anything-that-carries-out-a-mission\" target=\"_blank\">some other stuff</a> I was kind of already there, but it's good to see people making these connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T22:20:39-08:00","id":813183,"title":"","content":"All that's left is the Shard Chapter, and even then, just the last two.<br /> <br /> The crossover section was <i>excellent</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:03:26-08:00","id":813311,"title":"","content":"I found the stopgap 2e Geist rules to be particularly interesting in the crossover section.<br /> <br /> This book is making me really want to run a game of Demon.<br /> <br /> Which I suppose means it is fulfilling its intended purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:11:30-08:00","id":813417,"title":"","content":"As someone who is not a Demon fan but is a big Mummy fan I have to say, after getting to look over a friend's copy, the crossover section is excellent. Also while I don't think the themes of the game in general work for me, the cybercity setting hack portion was a very fun read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T21:14:22-08:00","id":813896,"title":"","content":"Who's the genius who referenced Utena in Fear Tomorrow? They are my new favorite person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:45:49-08:00","id":815011,"title":"","content":"A question for the sake of broad strokes usage: about how much Essence does fulfilling their Parameter give an exile? i.e. Are we looking at something in the neighborhood of 1 or [Rank] points, the results of a spirit-esque Power + Finesse roll, or a full top-up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:07:06-08:00","id":815024,"title":"","content":"I would assume it's equal to Rank, but don't quote me.<br /> <br /> Finished it yesterday. Damn I love everything in this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:50:07-08:00","id":815870,"title":"","content":"I am definitely on-board with Incepts.<br /> <br /> It really gives those big-picture powers that the Angels from the core book lacks, even if they're implied to have those cosmic tier powers from all the fiction. It's the last piece of the puzzle and it makes them work. It makes them <i>terrifying</i> too. They've got just enough breadth with the list there you could basically build up a set of Angels that'd do anything you want. It also will certainly make a Demon hesistant to tangle with any Angel, because you never know which one they might pull out if you lean on them too hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:31:16-08:00","id":816390,"title":"","content":"So far the only thing I haven't really liked is the Werewolf crossover section. Or parts of it, to be more precise. It makes sense that demons are inclined to see everything in the context of the God-Machine but it feels like there are some leaps of logic and needless conflations in comparison with Werewolves and the Idigam. They're not that egregious, but there's stuff suggested to be the dominant outlook of demons on features of WtF which seems very conspiracy theory-like. Not their perception of Luna's relationship with werewolves, but other parallels that are drawn.<br /> <br /> The Cipher elaboration and storytelling advices are magnificent, Incepts are impressive, slivers are a fascinating outcome for Exiles, and the setting shards have me salivating. The overwhelming majority of the crossover section is useful, fun and has some terrifying hooks (like the Strix's effect on Infrastructure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-25-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T14:41:26-08:00","id":816438,"title":"","content":"I love how Incepts supercharge other powers for the most part, and the idea that their use can be felt. For when you really want that Huner Angel's laser blast to annihilate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:59:13-08:00","id":817803,"title":"","content":"My favorite part of Incepts is that if you don't like them (I'm still torn) you can easily just skip them entirely! ::P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:56:55-08:00","id":818615,"title":"","content":"Is the errata for this finished? Because the following entry in the expanded inspirational material is simply wrong.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ghost in the Shell (1995, dir. Mamoru Oshii). A classic anime film exploration of where machine ends and soul begins. The series that serves as its sequel, Stand Alone Complex<br /> (2002-2005, directed by Kenji Kamiyama), expands on the problems of artificial intelligence that gains sapience.&quot;<br /> <br /> In point of fact, Oshii's '95 film (and it's '04 sequel <i>Innocence</i>) is one adaptation of the original <i>Ghost in the Shell </i>comic (manga) by Masamune Shirow. The <i>Stand Alone Complex</i> series is an alternate take on the same source material (and has its own sequel in movie form, the 2006 <i>Solid State Society</i>). <i>Ghost in the Shell: Arise</i> is yet a third adaptation of the same source material (and, most ironically spawned its own spin-off comic (manga)). <br /> <br /> Further while each of the versions explore the area of artificial intelligence gaining sapience the real focus is on exploring where the machine (your body) ends and the soul (or self) begins. The question posed is 'how do I know what I'm experiencing is real if all I am is a disembodied brain stuffed in a mechanical body suit?'<br /> <br /> Bonus trivia: This same topic of self-identity versus our corporeal existence also appears in the short series <i>Bubblegum Crisis</i> and A.D. Police Files.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:58:31-08:00","id":818659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=818615#post818615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the errata for this finished?</div> </div> </div> </div>The errata threads are closed and de-stickied once the collection period is over, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:25:28-08:00","id":818680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=818659#post818659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The errata threads are closed and de-stickied once the collection period is over, so yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah well, no sense in sweating it. The presence of some amount of errors is a reality of the publishing industry. Quick question though, is the section on Ciphers supposed to lead off with an &quot;in this chapter&quot; sentence? Did anyone catch that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:29:55-08:00","id":818739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=812945#post812945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, how does it fit in when there are several Demon powers that do point 2? Is it just a matter that with the Dynamic Legend option, every demon has an option for it?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I might as well drop my questions about powers here.<br /> <br /> 1)Angelic Reflexes has no duration listed.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Roll Power + Finesse \u2013 Subterfuge to determine if the humans within the angel\u2019s range notice what the angel is seeking.&quot; - so can angels see through the eyes of every person affected by Translocation, or what? How do they get that information? Also, what exactly happens when someone uses Translocation and a Demon spoofs it? They register as human but still can't be moved (or seen through, as above)? How do angels register that one?<br /> <br /> 3)What's the essence cost for Incepts that have a primary ability without a listed cost, like Economy, Efficiency, Units, etc?<br /> <br /> 4)Is there a cap on how many essence you can spend for Scale's primary effect? Are you only limited to Numina when using it, or can you apply it to whatever dice pools and modifiers you wish?<br /> <br /> 5)I've been trying to be objective here while I'm asking questions, but I have to ask: you can seriously use Space to obviate someone's Defense? :/<br /> <br /> 6) How does Scale work with powers that do multiple things, like Angelic Reflexes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Kirby, sorry I didn't see you questions edited into your post until now.<br /> <br /> 1) It lasts the scene. Since a combat is likely to be a scene, you could say it lasts for the duration of the conflict.<br /> <br /> 2) When activating Translocation, the angel taps into the general awareness patterns of every human in its range. Through this, it can identify the 'thought spike' that indicates a human has seen what it searches for. This isn't looking through the eyes of every human, or even reading their surface thoughts. Think about a time when you were somewhere public and unexpectedly saw someone you knew. That brief spike of recognition and the thrill of seeing them (or concern of having to avoid them) is what the angel looks for, but it has 'planted' the spike trigger condition across everyone. The angel will notice supernatural 'gaps' in its awareness and can sense when they interact with its human network, but doesn't know what they are unless it investigates further. Demons who successfully spoof against Translocation won't even be noticed by the angel. Their readout will seem human, and they won't have any 'spike' for the angel to latch onto.<br /> <br /> When the angel chooses to swap places with someone, it either homes in on the 'spike' (which means demons won't ever be targeted if the angel is looking for some trigger), or if the angel is simply wanting to move quickly though the area, it will always swap with some unsuspecting human in the area, and won't even consider how the Numen chose which random human it swapped with - it simply considers the spoofing demon a human that the power didn't choose. If a demon is the only being in an area where the angel wants to be, the Numen won't even spot her to require spoofing, and she's immune to the swapping power. If a demon was in an area with humans and successfully spoofed, and then every human in the area left, the Numen would register that every human had left and wouldn't notice the demon still there. Demons are a particular blind spot to Translocation. Additionally, Translocation relies on the presence of normal humans to notice anyone in an area at all. If everyone in a room had a supernatural tolerance rating, the angel would just register it as an empty room.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though 'demons' are a blind spot, a specific demon that the Angel knows the cover for, or one where the angel has something specific to latch onto is fair game. Here, the angel is relying on humans to notice the specifics, rather than generic 'demon'. So, an angel that knows lawyer 'Steve Johnson' is a Cover for Angel Damiel could make humans on range sensitive to the cover. Similarly, if the angel knows a demon in range has just taken possession of a specific object, it could home in on the object. It may get many false hits if the object is generic. 'I'm looking for the person carrying a red umbrella' will generate more false leads than 'I'm looking for the person carrying the red umbrella with white rose pattern and a silver handle'. <br /> <br /> 3) If they don't list a cost, they cost 0 Essence to use, just the Willpower to activate.<br /> <br /> 4) Incepts technically work according to the usual ephemeral being spending limits, ie, no more than what they currently have. If this is too much for a group, the ST may limit it to Rank+1 or Rank+2. Scale specifically calls out dice pools and Social maneuvering, it's applicable to more than Numina.<br /> <br /> 5) Yes, if the ST decides that the way the angel manifests the effect through Space prevents the target from defending.<br /> <br /> 6) If a power does multiple things for a single cost, Scale enhances all of them. If a power has multiple effects that are activated separately, Scale must be applied separately to each. For Angelic Reflexes, Scale enhances Initiative boost and Defense boost for a single cost.<br /> <br /> The possibility of an angel using Incepts should be terrifying, and should open up potentially massive displays of enormous power. Storytellers should be mindful that angels don't use Incepts lightly - these are the powers that destroy entire cities (or countries), or move comets from their orbits, but they're flashy and noticeable. Most of the time, the God-Machine hasn't authorised their use, and an angel simply wouldn't consider using them. They're the antithesis of the subtlety the GM usually prefers. An angel exercising its free will to use Incepts could potentially disrupt other subtle GM projects in an area, and is probably dangerously close to falling - in fact, demons who fell because they used awesome, noisy power for what they considered 'the right reasons' may make up a disproportionate percentage of Integrators who want to be allowed back in, never intended to rebel, and don't really understand what they did wrong.<br /> <br /> Incepts are a basic integrated design component of angels, incorporated back in ancient times when the GM needed to throw around awesome amounts of cosmic energy to create massive feats of planetary realignment and geoengineering. They're a design legacy that exists in the heart of every angel as a temptation to go beyond mission, and possibly fall. The GM would probably remove them from angels if it was capable of thinking about it and redesigned their core components. The fact that it hasn't either means that it can't, won't, or doesn't care about the loss of a few angels from pre-installed temptation subroutines. This could be an interesting philosophical point for angels and demons to consider for some chronicles.<br /> <br /> Incepts may be an 'I win' button for an angel, but their use usually means the God-Machine has already lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":"2) and fixing typos. 01-28-2016, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T06:30:53-08:00","id":820925,"title":"","content":"So, essentially incepts are the angelic equivalent of going loud?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T08:46:05-08:00","id":821019,"title":"","content":"Forgive me, but are Lares not supposed to have Influence, or is that getting fixed in errata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  A word 02-01-2016, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T23:38:57-08:00","id":821465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=820925#post820925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, essentially incepts are the angelic equivalent of going loud?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> From a conceptual basis, going loud came first, leading me to wonder 'why don't angels have anything similar? Where does this ability come from?' Within the game world, the legacy of demons former angelic existence, specifically having had access to Incepts, opens the capacity for them to go loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T15:02:58-08:00","id":821900,"title":"","content":"Updated storyteller's guide PDF seems to be out now. Guess that means we're gonna see the POD shortly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T15:16:24-08:00","id":821909,"title":"","content":"The numbers for Dalu form still don't work right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T17:15:53-08:00","id":821992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=821465#post821465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> From a conceptual basis, going loud came first, leading me to wonder 'why don't angels have anything similar? Where does this ability come from?' Within the game world, the legacy of demons former angelic existence, specifically having had access to Incepts, opens the capacity for them to go loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I understand the reasoning, and I like Incepts - them being a thing makes sense. But I don't see how the Incepts &gt; Go Loud connection holds.<br /> <br /> Incepts are something that comes from the God-Machine, something which may be inherent to the framework of every angel even if they're often not authorized to use it; they equate to their master system's acess codes to reality. Going Loud is a demon sacrificing a piece of infrastructure extremely vital to them, the one kind of infrastructure that they are able to use and build in such a way, for a burst of aetheric energy that momentarily expands <i>their </i>awareness of occult physics and integration with reality.<br /> <br /> On a somewhat different train of thought, isn't going loud by its own definition something demons alone can do, since the G-M spoonfeeds angels anything it thinks they need to know (how they make use of what they have and their degree of compliance to mission parameters nonwithstanding)? Even if they could do something truly comparable to going loud, wouldn't they instantly fall, making the point moot? It's been said that Incepts are a conspicuous temptation for Angels who hold thoughts of acting independently or deviating from orders, because they're always there as an option, and so are a very likely catalyst for the Fall. Is the relation drawn from that in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-02-2016, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:37:41-08:00","id":822461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=821019#post821019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me, but are Lares not supposed to have Influence, or is that getting fixed in errata?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. I'm unsure if this was intentional or a mistake on my part (I wrote this a long time ago), so use your own judgement. Incepts are similarly a your-judgement call, but I personally think they should have them. <br /> <br /> Actually, I have a few other Lares and Imperatives written up, I should post them sometime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T21:02:52-08:00","id":823047,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit sad none of the Angels included in the book have listed Incepts. Not that's it's hard to add them in or anything. Just incongruous with their introduction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T04:45:36-08:00","id":823228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=821992#post821992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, I understand the reasoning, and I like Incepts - them being a thing makes sense. But I don't see how the Incepts &gt; Go Loud connection holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll break this down into pieces and talk my way through the thinking process. Apologies if any of this is unclear, it's late here. Ask questions if what I've written below doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Although DtD is an espionage-themed game, demons are more than spies, they're hackers. In fact, demons are first and foremost hackers. They hack reality to get what they want, obscure their identities, and keep themselves one step ahead of the competition. Demons hack together Covers from whole cloth or fragments of actual code (ie, human lives), and they use these to hide from the system. When scrutinised, they spoof their authenticity, hoping that the legitimate agents of the system will think they're normal code and move on. Embeds are their use of back doors and inadvertent vulnerabilities in the code to force outcomes with minimal risk to themselves. Exploits are more brute force attacks where they pit their own hacking skills against the system and force it to bend in ways it's not really meant to work.<br /> <br /> The DSTG tells us that Exploits are the demonic extension of Incepts. 'A demon\u2019s Fall cancels her Incept privileges. She must hack together Aether-fueled Exploits in crude imitation of what she lost.' This is subtle, but important. When an angel falls, the God-Machine removes her Incept privileges. It scrambles her access codes to keep her out of the system, but it can't uninstall the essential hardware of the Incept component. Quintessential reality hackers, demons find workarounds that allow them to force Aether through the Incept 'gateway' to create the more limited Exploit effects. Even these severely curtailed effects cause noticeable Incept-like ripples, forcing the demon to test for compromise of her Cover.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that makes sense so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=821992#post821992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incepts are something that comes from the God-Machine, something which may be inherent to the framework of every angel even if they're often not authorized to use it; they equate to their master system's acess codes to reality. Going Loud is a demon sacrificing a piece of infrastructure extremely vital to them, the one kind of infrastructure that they are able to use and build in such a way, for a burst of aetheric energy that momentarily expands <i>their </i>awareness of occult physics and integration with reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where our interpretations differ, because this is a 'chicken-and-egg' scenario. The tl;dr version of the next couple of paragraphs is that you're saying 'the demon sacrifices her Cover to access power', whereas I'm saying 'the act of accessing the power destroys the Cover'. A subtle, but important difference to the thesis behind Incepts.<br /> <br /> Let's examine what Going Loud actually is from the point of view of what it does. You can read going loud as presented in DtD (p113) as 'demon drops Cover, gains massive power', but this kind of gets it backwards IMO. The key sentence on p113 is 'In a burst of raw, aetheric energy, the demon casts off her mortal shell and, for a brief, glorious moment, remembers what it was to be connected to the entire universe in a way she hasn't experienced since she served the God-Machine.' The key part of this sentence is 'in a burst of raw, aetheric energy'. It doesn't say she gains the energy from destroying the Cover, and I'd argue that since it's possible to discard a Cover without going loud (or making any sort of ripple), it's not the act of destroying a Cover that initiates the going loud benefits.<br /> <br /> The demon forces the universal machinery to accept her as one for a gloriously short period of time. She connects to the system in the most obvious way possible, and she knows it's going to be noticeable, and draw attention. She can't maintain a Cover under this, she's naked before the God-Machine. But even here her connection is an imperfect hack. Her power shoots up, maximising her potential possibly beyond what she was an a legitimate angel. She's filled with ephermeral fuel straight from the mains system, just like angels, but it's a quick top-up. She gains even more access to the system than angels, but because the hack is imperfect, her greater access is more limited than an angel's. An angel's version of 'going loud' is using whatever Incepts it has auhorised access to, even if it doesn't necessarily have tactic approval to deploy them. A demon's going loud gives access to every Exploit, even those that would logically have been hacked from Incepts she never had access to as an angel.<br /> <br /> To help visualise this, assume that the God-Machine installs every Incept into every angel when it is Outputted, but due to metaphysical limitations of the angelic form, it can only hold access codes to a number equal to its Rank. Any more would destroy it. (For a bonus bit of chronicle paranoia, this could logically mean that if an angel returns to refitting Infrastructure between missions, the God-Machine can swap out access codes to make the angel more suited to each mission. This means that an antagonist angel will not only return each time with a different power tool set, but may become more creative and closer to falling the longer the demons can string it along.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=821992#post821992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a somewhat different train of thought, isn't going loud by its own definition something demons alone can do, since the G-M spoonfeeds angels anything it thinks they need to know (how they make use of what they have and their degree of compliance to mission parameters nonwithstanding)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that by definition only demons can go loud, but that's because going loud is a specific term for the demonic version of tapping into power and using it, and it has a few side effects that other creatures don't experience. Other creatures have their own versions of tapping into power, with their own side effects. These aren't called going loud, but they're the equivalent. Angels use Incepts - they tap into power, they're noticeable, but they don't lose Cover or suffer the other problems demons do. To look at it from the other direction, demons go loud by activating the hacks that allow them to emulate angels as close as possible - they do this is by flicking every switch and connecting every circuit that taps into their residual Incept components and briefly lugs them back into the universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=821992#post821992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they could do something truly comparable to going loud, wouldn't they instantly fall, making the point moot? It's been said that Incepts are a conspicuous temptation for Angels who hold thoughts of acting independently or deviating from orders, because they're always there as an option, and so are a very likely catalyst for the Fall. Is the relation drawn from that in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Incepts are a temptation, but not an instant Fall trigger. Remember, Incepts are tools the God-Machine does install in its angels. It wants them to have the capacity, for its own inscrutable reasons. In today's word, the God-Machine's works are more subtle, and it doesn't want attention drawn to it. But in the (possible) distant past, Its angels used Incepts to move planets into alignment, alter orbits, and geo-engineer what It required. If you want to equate human misundersanding of the God-Machine with another deity, it authorised angels to use Incepts to flood the world, or transform entire cities into salt.<br /> <br /> Even in modern times, the God-Machine may authorise angels to use their Incepts. If a demonic ring becomes too obviously successful, they may find themselves tracked by a hunter-killer angel with orders to get the job done by any means necessary - including raining down fire on entire city blocks. Additionally, if a guardian uses Incepts to terminate a group of demons from disrupting a painstakingly constructed occult matrix - and it doesn't damage the Output - the God-Machine probably won't care. If the matrix is disrupted and the angel uses Incepts to track and destroy the guilty parties to ensure they can't do it again, the God-Machine may turn a blind eye. Similarly, if some working requires the collection and harvesting of supernatural creatures, and the angel tasked with this just uses its Incepts to bring the components to it, the God-Machine will probably be satisfied by a job done efficiently.<br /> <br /> And sometimes, an angel will use an Incept out of desperation, or oversight, or stupidity, and the God-Machine does nothing. What does that mean for its existence? Is it tacit permission that it should use the Incept again, or did it just get lucky this time. As much as it's a life of clarity, an angel's life can also be one of underlying confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T06:08:32-08:00","id":823270,"title":"","content":"I see one small problem here: If going loud merely destroys cover as a <i>side effect</i>, and not as fuel for the process itself, there would be no reason for them to be unable to do so while burned or in a temporary one, which is explicitly noted to not be possible to go loud from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T06:25:26-08:00","id":823283,"title":"","content":"I can see that our interpretations differ quite a bit, but I understand the reasoning now. I don't necessarily agree, particularly with the details, but it was a very constructive explanation. I was taking the connection you drew between incepts and exploits in too a literal a sense before, but from a concept standpoint and in mind of logical repercussions it makes sense. Thanks for taking the time to respond, Bunyip. That said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823270#post823270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see one small problem here: If going loud merely destroys cover as a <i>side effect</i>, and not as fuel for the process itself, there would be no reason for them to be unable to do so while burned or in a temporary one, which is explicitly noted to not be possible to go loud from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elfive got there first, but I was thinking the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-04-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:16:58-08:00","id":823529,"title":"","content":"Wildly Theorizing: You might need at least the barest minimum shreds of a Cover to even get close enough to flip the MOAR POWUR!1!! switch. Trying it &quot;naked&quot; (Burned) or in a temporary gets your hand smacked away from the cookie jar before you can do so (my apologies to all butchered metaphors harmed here)?<br /> <br /> Like, metaphysically speaking, Going Loud is a guarded room. Obviously Demons and Demons in the equivalent of a paste-on-mustache can't get access, but a Demon in Cover can walk on by (the obviously lax, but not non-existent, security) and enter. Sure, they are found out afterward, but at that point it doesn't matter anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-04-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:18:17-08:00","id":823532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823270#post823270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see one small problem here: If going loud merely destroys cover as a <i>side effect</i>, and not as fuel for the process itself, there would be no reason for them to be unable to do so while burned or in a temporary one, which is explicitly noted to not be possible to go loud from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needing a certain metaphysical distance to generate the aetheric buildup isn't interchangeable with burning the bridge used to cross that distance as fuel. Remember that overclocking is a concept that's built into how a fair number of demonic powers operate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:30:19-08:00","id":823603,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why a bridge is needed at all as opposed to the metaphysical fuel to actually pass a known threshold when the system being connected to isn't the God-Machine but rather the fabric of the universe (and that level of access then alerts it), but that's just my reading of the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:42:53-08:00","id":823621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823603#post823603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why a bridge is needed at all</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked an idiom that involves the severing of connections because that's literally what destroying a Cover does. Evidently this was an imperfect choice of metaphor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as opposed to the metaphysical fuel to actually pass a known threshold </div> </div> </div>Going loud requires for you to have built up enough an identity that you can jump from its apex to pierce its foundation and tap the infernal energies it's built on, which as a knock-on effect causes the building to collapse, if that topological analogy is clearer or more sensible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> when the system being connected to isn't the God-Machine but rather the fabric of the universe (and that level of access then alerts it), but that's just my reading of the corebook. </div> </div> </div>The Unchained are irrevocable connected to the God-Machine in metaphysical terms \u2014 their post-Fall adaptations specifically concern subverting its processes and the byproducts thereof and going loud only offers benefits that relate specifically to those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:50:25-08:00","id":823745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823621#post823621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picked an idiom that involves the severing of connections because that's literally what destroying a Cover does. Evidently this was an imperfect choice of metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first metaphor wasn't particularly obfuscating, I just took exception to the message.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823621#post823621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unchained are irrevocable connected to the God-Machine in metaphysical terms \u2014 their post-Fall adaptations specifically concern subverting its processes and the byproducts thereof and going loud only offers benefits that relate specifically to those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet they are no longer integrated with its systems and information. They rely on their own understanding of occult physics to use the same channels as the God-Machine and interface with the flaws of reality as independent subjects.<br /> <br /> Whether the Machine is responsible for the existence of those channels or it arose from them is a different matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-04-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:04:22-08:00","id":823755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823745#post823745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they rely on their own understanding of occult physics to use the same processes and byproducts thereof as the God-Machine</div> </div> </div> </div>Aether is by definition not something the God-Machine uses and Embeds are specifically pieces of occult-physics-under-the-God-Machine that the Unchained relearn in the regular course of events and gain unprecedented access to when going loud.<br /> <br /> &quot;Connecting to the fabric of the universe&quot; is not meaningfully distinct from connecting to the God-Machine's system of worldly manipulation as an explanation of power when all the benefits it affords a character are represented in terms of getting stuff that the God-Machine produces as a means of reclaiming a degree of their former angelic might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:15:34-08:00","id":823764,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Also, Primum and Aether are explicitely distinct from the operation and fuel of the God-Machine, and incredible boosts to both are tangible benefits of going loud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:23:48-08:00","id":823772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823764#post823764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aether [is] explicitely distinct from the operation and fuel of the God-Machine</div> </div> </div> </div>It literally cannot exist without the Machine, being a byproduct of its use of Essence.<br /> <br /> Primum is a measure of a demon's integration into reality as a separate being from the God-Machine rather than an extension thereof. This is not the same thing as having nothing to do with the Machine, particularly when heightened Primum comes with a greater capacity for manipulating Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:35:12-08:00","id":823786,"title":"","content":"One thing I've always wondered from a Storyteller's perspective, Numina and Embeds don't seem equivalent, or even remotely similar for that matter. However, Embeds are things Demons are remembering from their time as Angels no? How do you design the Angelic version of Embeds? Is it just making Numina powers or is it more like Influence? I was hoping to learn more about those mechanics in the Storytellers Guide, the game mechanical transition from Angel to Demon, but didn't find to much. Still very pleased though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:38:53-08:00","id":823791,"title":"","content":"That was poor recall of its exclusive origins on my part. Fair enough. I led myself into error there.<br /> <br /> I did not contest they were related to the God-Machine. I contested the meaning of going loud where it relates to the how of the power achieved by the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:40:08-08:00","id":823794,"title":"","content":"I'd say influence. Or just a regular roll. Angels are supposed to just do stuff like that all the time without really thinking about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:41:43-08:00","id":823797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823786#post823786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've always wondered from a Storyteller's perspective, Numina and Embeds don't seem equivalent, or even remotely similar for that matter. However, Embeds are things Demons are remembering from their time as Angels no? How do you design the Angelic version of Embeds? Is it just making Numina powers or is it more like Influence? I was hoping to learn more about those mechanics in the Storytellers Guide, the game mechanical transition from Angel to Demon, but didn't find to much. Still very pleased though!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don;t remember the page, but the core book talks about embeds replacing things that Angles do naturally, below the level of even Numina or Influences. More like their Skills and even more direct things like manifesting and exisiting in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:46:36-08:00","id":823804,"title":"","content":"Wow. I must have missed that... So you just have narrative freedom to have a Hunter Killer Angel roll a Rank or Skill check for a Just Bruised kind effect whenever? That's not only terrifying, but also a bit confusing. How would you run that as a Storyteller? Pick a suitable Embed and roll Rank + Skill reflexively if it's reflexive, or instant action if its not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:51:23-08:00","id":823928,"title":"","content":"Here's how you do it: Note in the Numina section like so<br /> <br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast, Just Bruised (As Embed), Awe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:05:09-08:00","id":823940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823928#post823928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how you do it: Note in the Numina section like so<br /> <br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast, Just Bruised (As Embed), Awe</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon corebook even has an example of this, although strangely enough, it's not for an angel, but the sample writeup of an intruder that might emerge from a dramatic failure at Raising Dead.<br /> <br /> Although I'd muse that the Embeds which the Unchained develop derive as much from narrower exercises of the principles that allowed them Influence as angels. An Influence over Silence is going to be able to cover much more ground than the use of Hush, but it's expensive, only practical because it can draw on the support of Essence provided by infrastructure conditions and sacrifices. The fallen angel who reverse-engineers Hush from that knowledge develops a narrower ability from what fine manipulation she can work on her own, without that support from the God-Machine's labors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T20:13:47-08:00","id":823968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823940#post823940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demon corebook even has an example of this, although strangely enough, it's not for an angel, but the sample writeup of an intruder that might emerge from a dramatic failure at Raising Dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also an example in How An Angel Dies; The Lambent has Shatter as a Numen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T20:34:52-08:00","id":823974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823755#post823755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aether is by definition not something the God-Machine uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there are examples of GM making infrastructure that specifically uses aether rather than having it as a byproduct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T20:54:15-08:00","id":823981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823974#post823974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely what I mean by &quot;the energies produced by the God-Machine as a byproduct of Its other activities are by definition neither energies that It uses to perform those operations nor conceptually independent from It.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T21:54:35-08:00","id":824003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823981#post823981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not remotely what I mean by &quot;the energies produced by the God-Machine as a byproduct of Its other activities are by definition neither energies that It uses to perform those operations nor conceptually independent from It.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's infrastructure that specifically uses aether as it's power source. So I'm not sure how that isn't being used to perform an operation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:07:34-08:00","id":824007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824003#post824003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's infrastructure that specifically uses aether as it's power source.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is Infrastructure that specifically recycles Aether into Essence, which is not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:18:07-08:00","id":824013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824007#post824007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is Infrastructure that specifically recycles Aether into Essence, which is not the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misremembering, there's infrastructure that turns essence into aether, and then that aether is used to power a separate set of weather manipulation infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:33:44-08:00","id":824022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824013#post824013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're misremembering, there's infrastructure that turns essence into aether, and then that aether is used to power a separate set of weather manipulation infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather difficult for me to misremember an ambiguously worded incidental statement about the Rainbow Serpent Stone that you've interpreted in a fashion that contradicts literally everything other source about the way Aether works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:42:36-08:00","id":824030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824022#post824022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather difficult for me to misremember an ambiguously worded incidental statement about the Rainbow Serpent Stone that you've interpreted in a fashion that contradicts literally everything other source about the way Aether works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware it contradicts how other examples of aether work, I actually asked if it was an error to someone at one point I think. But it's not really ambiguously worded at all... &quot;designed to siphon spirit energy (Essence) and transforms it into Aether, which is meant to power climate-control Infrastructure&quot;. It specifically siphons essence, turns it into aether, which then powers climate-control infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:49:42-08:00","id":824035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824030#post824030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not really ambiguously worded at all... &quot;designed to siphon spirit energy (Essence) and transforms it into Aether, which is meant to power climate-control Infrastructure&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ambiguity that reconciles with the way the process is established to work is that it can also be read &quot;though it is not currently doing so, the Rainbow Stone is designed to transform Essence into Aether; like all major undertakings of the Machine, this conversion process is meant to power Infrastructure, in this case the matrices responsible for climate control.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:29:58-08:00","id":824149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824035#post824035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ambiguity that reconciles with the way the process is established to work is that it can also be read &quot;though it is not currently doing so, the Rainbow Stone is designed to transform Essence into Aether; like all major undertakings of the Machine, this conversion process is meant to power Infrastructure, in this case the matrices responsible for climate control.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one interpretation I suppose, but it raises the question why they even mention it if transforming essence into aether so the aether powers is what happens to all infrastructure. I think it's more likely that it does what the text says it does, and it happens to be an oversight. But to be honest, doesn't matter much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-05-2016, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:58:14-08:00","id":824610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=823270#post823270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see one small problem here: If going loud merely destroys cover as a <i>side effect</i>, and not as fuel for the process itself, there would be no reason for them to be unable to do so while burned or in a temporary one, which is explicitly noted to not be possible to go loud from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons as hackers. There's a big difference between a system knowing that there's a hacker out there somewhere, trying to get in, and the system knowing who the hacker is, where she is, what tools she's using, and exactly which pathways she's going to try and use. The first is a demon with a Cover - even though the Cover burns from the power, the access attempt is obscured by the demon having a Cover. Once she's Burned, she's locked out.<br /> <br /> Whichever direction you approach this from, it doesn't invalidate my thesis. You can assume that the act of going loud requires burning the Cover to give it the metaphysical 'spark' to initiate the process and forge the connections to the system. If this is true, it's because the demon is trying to copy what she lost as an angel. When angels 'go loud' (not that they call it that) they simply spend a point of Willpower and use their Incepts. When a demon goes loud, it has to sacrifice something really important to try and copy the process. That's because demons are locked out of the toy box, and it sucks to be them. The price of freedom is that everything is more difficult.<br /> <br /> However, because the demon is forcing the issue, her emulation of the angelic process is different. Se burns her Cover, but when she plugs in, she <b>really </b>plugs in. Primum shoots through to max, access to powers she never had before etc. But it's a limited-time offer. All this power draw is a beacon to the God-Machine. One scene, that's all she gets, then the access is cut off and she can't attempt it again until she can shake off the pursuers and fool them about which direction she'll come from next time.<br /> <br /> If you don't agree, don't like, it, or don't like/want to use Incepts, that's fine. I'm just giving some insight into the thought process I followed when inventing the concept of Incepts. IF you like Incepts and want to rewrite where they come from and how they synch with demonic processes, that's fine too. From my point of view, I'd love if people use the material to make their games more fun (and their angelic antagonists more terrifying), and adapt the 'whys' and 'hows' to suit their own chronicle framework. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T15:30:08-08:00","id":824627,"title":"","content":"No, I really like the interpretation. It was just this one little incongruity that was bugging me, but your explanation makes total sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T05:13:26-08:00","id":824903,"title":"","content":"I think people mentally associate Incepts with Going Loud because both are really powerful things that tell the other side I'M HERE like a giant neon sign if they ever use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T04:33:32-08:00","id":825357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=824610#post824610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons as hackers. There's a big difference between a system knowing that there's a hacker out there somewhere, trying to get in, and the system knowing who the hacker is, where she is, what tools she's using, and exactly which pathways she's going to try and use. The first is a demon with a Cover - even though the Cover burns from the power, the access attempt is obscured by the demon having a Cover. Once she's Burned, she's locked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, I was close with my wild mass guessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:12:40-08:00","id":825642,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, you are my hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not the Beast kind of Hero. But the kind of hero that by just posting comments give me so many ideas to fill out and complete my chronicle. <br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:57:10-08:00","id":825826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=825642#post825642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunyip, you are my hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not the Beast kind of Hero. But the kind of hero that by just posting comments give me so many ideas to fill out and complete my chronicle.<br /> <br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I could help. And thank you for the feedback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:49:02-08:00","id":846463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/591980-demon-storyteller-s-guide?p=813896#post813896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's the genius who referenced Utena in Fear Tomorrow? They are my new favorite person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was going to ask where to find this....but its less than subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:14:18-08:00","id":846468,"title":"","content":"It's the level of subtlety I use.<br /> <br /> Which is about as subtle as a billboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:46:20-07:00","id":846712,"title":"","content":"I think I may have just gotten my hopes up too high thinking about what thing about the end of the world could be lifted from Utena. I went in expecting to hear something about chicks, shells, and smashing the world so that it can be born. <br /> <br /> Still, I'm always down for this sick beat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GRsWNBW_Mkc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GRsWNBW_Mkc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GRsWNBW_Mkc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GRsWNBW_Mkc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:47:48-07:00","id":846714,"title":"","content":"Of course, now that the authors have thrown in that reference, I wonder once again if &quot;Flowers of Hell&quot; viz the Player's Guide isn't a reference to Higurashi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014